import numpy as np
DESCRIPTION = ("TASK: the network reports the POSITION of the SECOND-LARGEST of the 10 inputs. "
 "Units with big input weights (units 1,4,6,7,8 have Wx=-10.6,+10.2,-11.0,-13.2,-12.3) are comparators: the state carries the "
 "running best value, so relu(Wx*x_t + Wh memory) fires exactly when the new input beats (unit 4) or loses to (unit 7) the "
 "carried value; the small units integrate those comparison events into a position code that the readout turns into a "
 "per-position class score. "
 "Step 1 is exactly rank 2: h1 = relu(x0*Wx) = 0.5*(|x0|*|Wx| + x0*Wx). "
 "Step 2 is exactly a function of (x1,|x0|,x0): h2 = relu(x1*Wx + |x0|*A + x0*B), so its range is the cone generated by "
 "relu(Wx +/- (A+B)); 7 coordinates on that cone carry everything later. "
 "Step 3: its pre-activation lives in the 8-dimensional fan {Wx, Q2@Wh}, so h3 = relu(z3) needs only 10 gate coordinates "
 "relu(Gs@c) on that fan (c a sign pattern, written as integers). "
 "The recurrent matrix is sparse: 212 of 256 entries carry the computation, the rest are exactly zero; likewise the readout "
 "keeps only 130 of its 160 entries. Readout: only class-score DIFFERENCES matter, so column 0 of Wo is subtracted off.")
